---
title: Lentil & Bulgur Pilaf
author: Jonathan Simmonds
servings: 6
---

Cook @green lentils{200%g} for ~{15%minutes} and set aside.

Heat @extra virgin olive oil{3%tbsp} in a #pan{} and sauté @onion{2}(finely diced) and @green pepper{1}(finely diced) and @red pepper{1}(finely diced) for ~{10%minutes} until soft.

Add @garlic{3%clove}(crushed) and @tomato puree{3%tbsp} and cook for ~{1%minutes}.

Add @bulgur wheat{250%g}, the cooked lentils, and @paprika{2%tsp} and @nutmeg{0.5%tsp} and cook for ~{2%minutes}, stirring occasionally.

Add @water{500%ml} and reduce to lowest heat, cover, and cook for ~{15%minutes} until absorbed.

Remove from heat and let it rest, covered, for ~{15%minutes}.

Fluff and serve.

> Pairs well with @./dinners/roasted-cauliflower-with-tahini{1}.
